# Configuration for the arcint systemd unit. Every arcint setting is a command
# line flag; this file exists so the unit itself does not have to be edited to
# change one.

ARCINT_MODEL=/models/ov/qwen36-coder-b5-ov
ARCINT_DEVICE=GPU.0
ARCINT_HOST=127.0.0.1
ARCINT_PORT=8081
ARCINT_N_CTX=262144
ARCINT_PREFIX_CACHE_MIB=8192

# Anything else, verbatim. Both speculative paths are off by default and are a
# net loss until the paged decode path lands (DESIGN §3.5.1–3.5.2), so they are
# deliberately not enabled here.
#   --mtp on              the Qwen3.8 MTP head, where the export carries one
#   --draft 4             prompt-lookup drafting
#   --custom-kernels ...  hand-written OpenCL (measurement switch)
#   --parallel 2          two client sessions at once (DESIGN §4.1). It is a
#                         memory claim as much as a flag: the reservation has to
#                         hold two lanes at ARCINT_N_CTX or the service refuses
#                         to start, with the arithmetic. Left at 1 here because
#                         this unit runs at the artifact's full 262144 context.
#   --queue-timeout 30    wait for a lane instead of a 503 when all are busy
#
# --queue-timeout is set below rather than left at its default. The engine
# default is 0 -- refuse a request that finds no free lane, with the reservation
# numbers -- because a lane is a memory claim and an unbounded queue is
# indistinguishable from a hang. For a *service* endpoint the older behaviour is
# the kinder one: an OpenAI-compatible client generally does not retry a 503, so
# a second concurrent caller would simply fail where it used to wait.
ARCINT_EXTRA_ARGS=--cache-dir /home/mfritsche/.cache/arcint --queue-timeout 30
